<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%= render partial: 'shared/assets' %>
<body class="bg-gray-dark color-white">
<div class="min-h-100 d-flex flex-column align-items-center justify-content-center">
	<div class="w-100 mb-3">
		<%= render partial: 'shared/menu', locals: {active: "about", appearance: "light"} %>
	</div>
	<div class="row w-100 m-auto">
		<div class="col-12">
			<div class="heading text-center">
				<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			</div>
			<div class="col-12 mb-3">
				<div class="col-lg-6 col-sm-10 col-xs-12 m-auto">
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
						This policy explains how personal data is handled by <%= @privacy_policy.service_url %>,
						the Readersourcing service operated by <%= @privacy_policy.controller_name %>.
					</p>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						The data controller can be contacted at
						<a href="mailto:<%= @privacy_policy.contact_email %>"><%= @privacy_policy.contact_email %></a>
						or through the contact form provided below.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Data We Process</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb"><strong>Account data:</strong> name, email address, password hash, optional ORCID, and email preference;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb"><strong>Readersourcing data:</strong> ratings, their dates, and their association with readers and publications;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb"><strong>Publication data:</strong> source addresses, bibliographic information, and copies of PDFs that a reader asks the service to prepare;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify"><strong>Service data:</strong> authentication records, IP addresses and request information in technical logs, and the email address and text supplied through the contact form.</p></li>
					</ul>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Passwords are stored only as password hashes. Readersourcing does not collect payment data and does not use the service data for advertising.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Purposes and Legal Bases</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">The data is processed for the following purposes:</p>
					<ul>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">to create and manage a reader account, authenticate requests, prepare publications, collect ratings, and compute Readersourcing scores, as necessary to provide the service requested by the reader under Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">to send registration, password recovery, rating confirmation, and service messages requested by the reader under Article 6(1)(b) of the GDPR;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">to answer questions and bug reports under Article 6(1)(b) or Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR, depending on the request;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">to prevent abuse, protect accounts, diagnose faults, and preserve the security and integrity of the service under the legitimate interests described in Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify">to comply with an applicable legal obligation under Article 6(1)(c) of the GDPR.</p></li>
					</ul>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Readersourcing does not send marketing newsletters and does not perform advertising profiling or automated decisions that produce legal or similarly significant effects.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Cookies</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						The web interface uses only the encrypted Rails session cookie needed to authenticate the reader, protect form submissions, and retain the current rating workflow. It is an essential technical cookie, is marked <code>HttpOnly</code>, and is sent securely when HTTPS is enabled. Readersourcing does not install analytics, advertising, preference, or social network cookies. Refusing the session cookie prevents the authenticated web interface from working, but does not add any other tracking.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Recipients and Processing Locations</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
						The service is hosted by <%= @privacy_policy.hosting_provider %> in <%= @privacy_policy.hosting_country %>. Email is delivered through <%= @privacy_policy.email_provider %> in <%= @privacy_policy.email_provider_country %>. These providers process only the data needed to supply infrastructure, database, backup, and email services on behalf of the controller.
					</p>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Personal data is not sold. It may be disclosed when required by law or when necessary to protect the service and its users. If a provider processes data outside the European Economic Area, the controller uses an adequacy decision or another safeguard permitted by Chapter V of the GDPR.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Retention and Deletion</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">Account information, ratings, authentication records, and PDFs prepared for a reader are retained while the account exists. Deleting the account removes the reader, ratings, active authentication records, and private publication copies associated with that reader;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">authentication tokens expire after seven days and password reset links expire after four hours;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">technical logs are retained for no more than <%= @privacy_policy.log_retention_days %> days, unless a longer period is required to investigate a security event or comply with law;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify no-mb">backup copies expire within <%= @privacy_policy.backup_retention_days %> days and are used only for recovery;</p></li>
						<li><p class="lead text-justify">contact messages are not stored in the Readersourcing database. They remain with the configured email provider only as long as needed to answer the request and meet any applicable legal obligation.</p></li>
					</ul>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Publication records are shared by the service and may remain after one reader deletes an account, but that reader's ratings and private PDF copies are removed.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Security</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Readersourcing uses password hashing, expiring authentication records, request limits, HTTPS in public deployments, restricted private storage, and signed PDF download links. No Internet service can guarantee absolute security, but access is limited to what is needed to operate and maintain the service.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Your Rights</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
						Under the GDPR, a reader may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, portability, or objection where the corresponding conditions apply. Consent, where used for a separate optional purpose, may be withdrawn without affecting earlier lawful processing.
					</p>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-3">
						Requests can be sent to the controller using the contact details above. A reader may also lodge a complaint with the
						<a href="https://www.garanteprivacy.it/">Italian Data Protection Authority</a> or another competent supervisory authority.
					</p>

					<h2 class="heading mb-3">Changes and Contact</h2>
					<p class="lead text-justify mb-2">
						Material changes will be published on this page with a revised effective date. The effective date of this policy is
						<time datetime="<%= @privacy_policy.effective_date.iso8601 %>"><%= @privacy_policy.effective_date.strftime("%B %d, %Y") %></time>.
					</p>
					<p class="lead text-justify">
						<a href="<%= contact_path %>" class="btn btn-primary">contact form</a>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
	<div class="row w-100 mt-3">
		<%= render partial: "shared/footer" %>
	</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
